=== FINDING (why this is FAIL) ===
Criterion 2's test does not discriminate on the loader's hash VALUE, so the
core mechanism of the feature is unguarded.

  MUTATION (independently reproduced by me, matching the adversarial
  checker's finding): in analysisFastOrCached,
      return a, depHash, nil   ->   return a, depHash + "x", nil
  This is the "loader div renders with the wrong hash" attack. In production
  it means the rendered loader's own GET can never match the current dep-hash,
  so it 204s forever and the pending skeleton hangs permanently -- a silent,
  total failure of fast-first.

  Ran the FULL attempt-1 package suite against it:
      go test ./internal/handlers/whatif/ -count=1
      -> ok  budget2/internal/handlers/whatif  11.442s   (EXIT 0)
  MUTATION SURVIVED. TestCalculateCacheMissRendersFastWithLoader only checks
  strings.Contains(body, "/whatif/results-full?hash=") -- a prefix that a
  corrupted or empty hash still satisfies. TestPollCacheMissRendersPending
  only checks the div's id. Every results-full test feeds its own
  independently-computed hash straight to the handler, bypassing the rendered
  value, so no test ever round-trips render -> endpoint.

  The shipped attempt-1 code is CORRECT (`return a, depHash, nil`); there is
  no live user-facing bug. The defect is test discrimination, which is
  precisely what this check exists to certify, and my instructions gate PASS
  on mutation probes being killed. One was not.

  CONFIRMATION the gap is real and attempt-1-specific: I applied the identical
  mutation to the current (attempt-2) worktree and it is killed by three
  tests -- TestCalculateCacheMissRendersFastWithLoader,
  TestPollCacheMissRendersPending, and the new
  TestPendingLoaderHashRoundTripsToFullResults. So the remedy is already
  written; it is simply not part of attempt 1.

WHAT IS MISSING (for the worker, not for me to fix): in
internal/handlers/whatif/results_full_test.go, extract the hash from the
rendered loader (regexp on hx-get="/whatif/results-full?hash=([^"]+)") and
assert EQUALITY with the buildEngineInput dep-hash for the same settings, in
both TestCalculateCacheMissRendersFastWithLoader and
TestPollCacheMissRendersPending; and round-trip that extracted hash through
handleWhatIfResultsFull expecting 200.

All mutations were applied only in scratch copies. `diff -r` confirmed the
mut copy was restored to the attempt-1 state after each probe, and the
pristine copy matches the worktree (web/ IDENTICAL; internal/ differs only by
the attempt-2 test additions that landed after my snapshot).
